id: stack/image-only
name: The image crate is the only third-party dependency
prose: "The wish fixes the stack as the executor's constraint: Rust with cargo, the image crate for reading and decoding, and no other third-party dependencies. The row pins the dependency declaration of Cargo.toml byte for byte: the [dependencies] section to the end of the file names image alone, so any added crate turns the row red. Cargo.lock sits in the scope, so a changed dependency graph re-runs the pin. The same declaration is what keeps the program off the network: the linked set is the standard library plus the image decode chain, nothing network-capable.\n"
scope:
- Cargo.toml
- Cargo.lock
covers:
- R1
rows:
- run: "sed -n '/^\\[dependencies\\]/,$p' Cargo.toml"
  expect:
    rc: 0
    out: "[dependencies]\nimage = { version = \"0.25.10\", default-features = false, features = [\"jpeg\"] }\n"
